Support pandas StringDtype in numeric-string cleaning

Downstream compatibility fix for retained oipd 1.0.2; not submitted upstream.
Pandas 3 infers StringDtype instead of object for strings. Keep the original
object-dtype branch and extend it only to pandas.StringDtype, applying the
same comma removal and numeric conversion. No pricing behavior changes.

Original code: https://github.com/Open-Lemma/options-implied-probability/blob/v1.0.2/oipd/io/reader.py
Upstream HEAD 180748f6a78e1eef22794add0de55e1d775be47e still has the object-only guard.

--- a/oipd/io/reader.py
+++ b/oipd/io/reader.py
@@ -150,5 +150,7 @@
         for col in columns_to_clean:
             # Handle string columns that might have commas in numbers
-            if raw_data[col].dtype == "object":
+            if raw_data[col].dtype == "object" or isinstance(
+                raw_data[col].dtype, pd.StringDtype
+            ):
                 # Remove commas from numeric strings (e.g., "1,200" -> "1200")
